---
title: Oat Flour Banana Muffins
servings: 12
cuisine: american
main_protein: none
prep_time: "10 minutes"
cook_time: "20 minutes"
tags:
  - breakfast
  - banana
  - oatflour
  - muffins
source: https://choosingchia.com/oat-flour-banana-muffins/
image: ../obsidian/attachments/oat-flour-banana-muffins.jpg
leftover_portions: 8
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 350°F
  - Line a muffin pan with liners
  - Mash 3 bananas
  - Bring 2 eggs to room temperature
---

Preheat #oven{} to 350°F and line a #muffin pan{} with muffin liners.

Combine @bananas{3}, mashed (about 1 cup), @eggs{2}, at room temperature, @avocado oil{0.33%cup} (or vegetable or canola oil), @maple syrup{0.33%cup} (or honey), and @vanilla extract{1%tsp} in a #large mixing bowl{} and mix until well combined.

In a separate bowl, mix together @oat flour{1.75%cups}, @baking soda{1%tsp}, @salt{0.25%tsp}, @cinnamon{0.5%tsp}, and @nutmeg{0.5%tsp}.

Add dry ingredients to wet ingredients and gently fold together until combined.

Add @chocolate chips{0.5%cup} and mix together.

Spoon batter into muffin pan, filling each liner 3/4 of the way full.

Bake for ~{18%minutes} to 22 minutes.
